findings.body:
Password reset tokens must be unpredictable. This replaces `randomBytes(32)` (256-bit CSPRNG) with `Math.floor(Math.random() * 1e12).toString(36)`, which is not cryptographically secure and has only ~40 bits of keyspace (~10^12 values, ~9 base-36 chars). An attacker can brute-force or predict tokens and take over accounts.

For edge runtimes, use Web Crypto instead of `Math.random`:

```suggestion
  const bytes = new Uint8Array(32);
  crypto.getRandomValues(bytes);
  return Array.from(bytes, (b) => b.toString(16).padStart(2, "0")).join("");
```

`globalThis.crypto.getRandomValues` is available on Cloudflare Workers, Vercel Edge, Deno, and Node 19+.
